-- title:
--   §1.2–§3, §6.3, pp. 3590–3609 — graphons, 𝒞_d, W₂, the class ℳ, the continuum noise, solutions of (2.1) and (3.1), Conditions 2.1, 2.3, 3.2, the terms of (6.16)
-- statement:
--   This file fixes the objects of Bayraktar, Chakraborty and Wu, *Graphon mean field systems* (Ann. Appl. Probab. 2023), used to state the uniform rate of convergence of Theorem 3.2.
--
--   **Labels and graphons.** Let $I=[0,1]$ with Lebesgue measure. A **graphon** is a measurable symmetric function $G:I\times I\to[0,1]$. Particle $i\in\{1,\dots,n\}$ carries the label $i/n\in I$. The file also records the cut norm $\|W\|_\square=\sup_{S,T}\left|\int_{S\times T}W(u,v)\,du\,dv\right|$ over Borel $S,T\subseteq I$, the operator norm $\|W\|_{\infty\to1}$, the step point $\lceil nu\rceil/n$ and step graphons, which are shared with the other missions of the series.
--
--   **Paths and laws.** Fix a horizon $T\in(0,\infty)$. $\mathcal C_d=C([0,T]:\mathbb R^d)$ carries the uniform norm $\|x\|_{*,T}=\sup_{0\le s\le T}|x_s|$ and its Borel $\sigma$-algebra. For two processes $X,Y$ and $t\in[0,T]$, $\|X-Y\|_{*,t}=\sup_{0\le s\le t}|X(s)-Y(s)|\in[0,\infty]$. The law $\mathcal L(X)\in\mathcal P(\mathcal C_d)$ of a process with continuous paths is the image of the underlying probability under $\omega\mapsto X(\cdot,\omega)$. $W_2$ is the Wasserstein-2 distance on $\mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$ and $W_{2,T}$ the one on $\mathcal P(\mathcal C_d)$ for the norm $\|\cdot\|_{*,T}$:
--   $$W_{2,T}(\mu,\nu)=\Big(\inf\{\mathbb E\|X-\tilde X\|_{*,T}^2:\mathcal L(X)=\mu,\ \mathcal L(\tilde X)=\nu\}\Big)^{1/2}.$$
--   The class $\mathcal M$ consists of families $(\nu_u)_{u\in I}$ of probability measures on $\mathcal C_d$ such that $u\mapsto\nu_u$ is measurable and $\sup_u\int\|x\|_{*,T}^2\,\nu_u(dx)<\infty$.
--
--   **Noise.** On a probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal F,\mathbb P)$, $\{B_u:u\in I\}$ are i.i.d. standard $d$-dimensional Brownian motions, $X_u(0)$ has law $\mu_u(0)$, and the whole family $\{X_u(0)\}_{u\in I}\cup\{B_u\}_{u\in I}$ is mutually independent.
--
--   **The graphon particle system (2.1).** $X=(X_u)_{u\in I}$ solves
--   $$X_u(t)=X_u(0)+\int_0^t\!\!\int_I\!\int_{\mathbb R^d}b(X_u(s),x)G(u,v)\,\mu_{v,s}(dx)\,dv\,ds+\int_0^t\!\!\int_I\!\int_{\mathbb R^d}\sigma(X_u(s),x)G(u,v)\,\mu_{v,s}(dx)\,dv\,dB_u(s),$$
--   with $\mu_{u,t}=\mathcal L(X_u(t))$, when every path is continuous, the law family $(\mathcal L(X_u))_u$ lies in $\mathcal M$, and each $X_u$ is a strong solution driven by $B_u$ for the filtration generated by $X_u(0)$ and $B_u$.
--
--   **The $n$-particle system (3.1).** $X^n=(X^n_1,\dots,X^n_n)$ solves
--   $$X^n_i(t)=X_{i/n}(0)+\int_0^t\frac1n\sum_{j=1}^n\xi^n_{ij}\,b(X^n_i(s),X^n_j(s))\,ds+\int_0^t\frac1n\sum_{j=1}^n\xi^n_{ij}\,\sigma(X^n_i(s),X^n_j(s))\,dB_{i/n}(s),$$
--   with the same initial states and Brownian motions as the continuum particles at the labels $i/n$, for the filtration generated by the weights, the initial states and the Brownian motions.
--
--   **Conditions.**
--   1. *Condition 2.1* (with $\varepsilon>0$): $u\mapsto\mu_u(0)$ is measurable, $\sup_u\mathbb E|X_u(0)|^{2+\varepsilon}<\infty$, and $|b(x,y)-b(x',y')|+|\sigma(x,y)-\sigma(x',y')|\le K(|x-x'|+|y-y'|)$.
--   2. *Condition 2.3*: for some $\kappa\in(0,\infty)$ and finitely many intervals $I_1,\dots,I_N$ covering $I$, $W_2(\mu_{u_1}(0),\mu_{u_2}(0))\le\kappa|u_1-u_2|$ for $u_1,u_2\in I_i$, and $|G(u_1,v_1)-G(u_2,v_2)|\le\kappa(|u_1-u_2|+|v_1-v_2|)$ for $(u_1,v_1),(u_2,v_2)\in I_i\times I_j$.
--   3. *Condition 3.2*: either (i) $\xi^n_{ij}=G(i/n,j/n)$ for all $n,i,j$, or (ii) for all $n$, $\xi^n_{ij}=\xi^n_{ji}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(G(i/n,j/n))$ independently for $1\le i\le j\le n$, and independent of $\{B_u,X_u(0):u\in I\}$.
--
--   **The terms of (6.16).** For particle $i$ and time $s$,
--   $$\tilde T^{n,1}_s=\mathbb E\Big|\frac1n\sum_j\xi^n_{ij}\big(b(X^n_i(s),X^n_j(s))-b(X_{i/n}(s),X_{j/n}(s))\big)\Big|^2,$$
--   $$\tilde T^{n,2}_s=\mathbb E\Big|\frac1n\sum_j\Big(\xi^n_{ij}b(X_{i/n}(s),X_{j/n}(s))-\int b(X_{i/n}(s),x)G(\tfrac in,\tfrac jn)\mu_{j/n,s}(dx)\Big)\Big|^2,$$
--   $$\tilde T^{n,3}_s=\mathbb E\Big|\frac1n\sum_j\int b(X_{i/n}(s),x)G(\tfrac in,\tfrac jn)\mu_{j/n,s}(dx)-\int_I\!\int b(X_{i/n}(s),x)G(\tfrac in,v)\mu_{v,s}(dx)\,dv\Big|^2.$$
--
--   These objects are the common vocabulary of every statement of the mission.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** $\mathbb R^d$ is `Fin d → ℝ` with the sup norm and $\sigma$ is measured entrywise (max norm); every statement of the paper is invariant under the choice of norm because every constant is existential. Particle $i$ is Lean's `i : Fin n` with label $(i+1)/n$. Time is `ℝ≥0`. The SDEs use the published Itô-process predicate `Peng1990.SMP.IsItoProcess` applied to $X-X(0)$ with zero initial value, for uncompleted natural filtrations; measurability of $u\mapsto\nu_u$ uses Mathlib's Giry $\sigma$-algebra, which on the Polish space $\mathcal C_d$ is the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of the weak topology. Membership of the law family in $\mathcal M$ is part of the solution predicate (Proposition 2.1 asserts it, and it makes the inner integrals meaningful). Expectations of nonnegative quantities are lower Lebesgue integrals in $[0,\infty]$, and $W_2$, $W_{2,T}$ are the published `WassersteinDRO.Duality.wassersteinDistance 2`. The intervals of Condition 2.3 are order-connected subsets of $I$ (any interval, possibly degenerate). In case (ii) the weights are $\{0,1\}$-valued and measurable, with $\mathbb P(\xi^n_{ij}=1)=G(i/n,j/n)$, and the diagonal $i=j$ is included.
-- source:
--   Bayraktar, Chakraborty, Wu, Graphon mean field systems, Ann. Appl. Probab. 33(5) (2023), https://doi.org/10.1214/22-AAP1901, pp. 3590–3596, §1.2, §2 (2.1)–(2.5), Conditions 2.1, 2.3, §3 (3.1), (3.2), Condition 3.2; p. 3609, (6.16)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Peng1990_SMP_Stochastic
import Definitions.Def_WassersteinDRO_Duality_wassersteinDistance
import Definitions.Def_GraphonMF_Stability_Setting

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology unitInterval
open scoped ENNReal NNReal

namespace GraphonMF.DenseRate

/-! ### Labels and graphons (§2, p. 3590; (3.2), p. 3595) -/

/-- The label `(i + 1)/n ∈ I` of particle `i : Fin n` (the paper's particle `i + 1 ∈ {1, …, n}`). -/
noncomputable def lab (n : ℕ) (i : Fin n) : I :=
  Set.projIcc 0 1 zero_le_one (((i : ℕ) + 1 : ℝ) / n)

/-- The step point `⌈n u⌉ / n ∈ I`. -/
noncomputable def stepPt (n : ℕ) (u : I) : I :=
  Set.projIcc 0 1 zero_le_one ((⌈(n : ℝ) * u⌉ : ℝ) / n)

/-- A graphon: a measurable symmetric function `I × I → [0, 1]`. -/
def IsGraphon (G : I → I → ℝ) : Prop :=
  Measurable (Function.uncurry G) ∧ (∀ u v, G u v = G v u) ∧ ∀ u v, G u v ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1

/-- The cut norm `‖W‖_□ = sup_{S,T Borel} |∫_{S×T} W(u,v) du dv|`. -/
noncomputable def cutNorm (W : I → I → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ⨆ (S : Set I) (T : Set I) (_ : MeasurableSet S ∧ MeasurableSet T),
    |∫ p in S ×ˢ T, W p.1 p.2|

/-- The operator norm `‖W‖_{∞→1} = sup_{‖g‖_∞ ≤ 1} ∫_I |∫_I W(u,v) g(v) dv| du` (Remark 2.1). -/
noncomputable def opNorm (W : I → I → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ⨆ (g : I → ℝ) (_ : Measurable g ∧ ∀ v, |g v| ≤ 1), ∫ u, |∫ v, W u v * g v|

/-- A step graphon (3.2): `G_n(u,v) = G_n(⌈nu⌉/n, ⌈nv⌉/n)`. -/
def IsStepGraphon (n : ℕ) (Gn : I → I → ℝ) : Prop :=
  IsGraphon Gn ∧ ∀ u v, Gn u v = Gn (stepPt n u) (stepPt n v)

/-! ### Paths, laws and Wasserstein distances (§1.2, (2.3)–(2.5), p. 3592) -/

instance (T : ℝ≥0) (d : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace (GraphonMF.Stability.Cd T d) := borel _

instance (T : ℝ≥0) (d : ℕ) : BorelSpace (GraphonMF.Stability.Cd T d) := ⟨rfl⟩

/-- `‖x‖_{*,t} = sup_{0 ≤ s ≤ t} |x_s|` for a path `x ∈ 𝒞_d`. -/
noncomputable def supUpTo {T : ℝ≥0} {d : ℕ} (t : ℝ≥0) (x : GraphonMF.Stability.Cd T d) : ℝ :=
  ⨆ s : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ≥0) T, if (s : ℝ≥0) ≤ t then ‖x s‖ else 0

/-- `sup_{0 ≤ s ≤ t} |X(s,ω) − Y(s,ω)|` for two processes, in `[0, ∞]`; for continuous
processes and `t ≤ T` this is `‖X(ω) − Y(ω)‖_{*,t}`. -/
noncomputable def supDistUpTo {Ω : Type*} {d : ℕ} (t : ℝ≥0)
    (X Y : ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (ω : Ω) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨆ (s : ℝ≥0) (_ : s ≤ t), ‖X s ω - Y s ω‖ₑ

open Classical in
/-- The path `ω ↦ X(·, ω)|_{[0,T]} ∈ 𝒞_d` of a process (the zero path if it is not continuous). -/
noncomputable def pathOf {Ω : Type*} {d : ℕ} (T : ℝ≥0) (X : ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (ω : Ω) :
    GraphonMF.Stability.Cd T d :=
  if h : Continuous (fun s : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ≥0) T => X s ω) then ⟨fun s => X s ω, h⟩ else 0

/-- The law `ℒ(X) ∈ 𝒫(𝒞_d)` of a process with continuous paths. -/
noncomputable def law {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (T : ℝ≥0) (P : Measure Ω)
    (X : ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) : Measure (GraphonMF.Stability.Cd T d) :=
  P.map (pathOf T X)

/-- `W₂` on `𝒫(ℝᵈ)` (2.3). -/
noncomputable def W2 {d : ℕ} (μ ν : Measure (Fin d → ℝ)) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  WassersteinDRO.Duality.wassersteinDistance 2 μ ν

/-- `W_{2,T}` on `𝒫(𝒞_d)` ((2.4) with `t = T`). -/
noncomputable def W2T {T : ℝ≥0} {d : ℕ} (μ ν : Measure (GraphonMF.Stability.Cd T d)) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  WassersteinDRO.Duality.wassersteinDistance 2 μ ν

/-- The class `ℳ` (p. 3592): measurable families `u ↦ ν_u ∈ 𝒫(𝒞_d)` with
`sup_u ∫ ‖x‖²_{*,T} ν_u(dx) < ∞`. -/
def InM {T : ℝ≥0} {d : ℕ} (ν : I → Measure (GraphonMF.Stability.Cd T d)) : Prop :=
  Measurable ν ∧ (∀ u, IsProbabilityMeasure (ν u)) ∧ (⨆ u, ∫⁻ x, ‖x‖ₑ ^ 2 ∂(ν u)) < ⊤

/-! ### The continuum noise (§1, §2, p. 3591) -/

/-- The σ-algebras generated by `X_u(0)` (left summand) and by `B_u` (right summand). -/
abbrev noiseFam {Ω : Type*} {d : ℕ} (X0 : I → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (B : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin d → ℝ) :
    I ⊕ I → MeasurableSpace Ω
  | Sum.inl u => MeasurableSpace.comap (X0 u) inferInstance
  | Sum.inr u => MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω t => B u t ω) inferInstance

/-- The σ-algebra `σ(X_u(0), B_u : u ∈ I)`. -/
abbrev noiseSigma {Ω : Type*} {d : ℕ} (X0 : I → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (B : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin d → ℝ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ k, noiseFam X0 B k

/-- The continuum noise: `{B_u : u ∈ I}` are i.i.d. standard `d`-dimensional Brownian motions,
`X_u(0)` has law `μ_u(0)`, and the family `{X_u(0)} ∪ {B_u}` is mutually independent. -/
structure NoiseSetting {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (P : Measure Ω)
    (μ0 : I → Measure (Fin d → ℝ)) (X0 : I → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (B : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin d → ℝ) : Prop where
  prob : IsProbabilityMeasure P
  meas_X0 : ∀ u, Measurable (X0 u)
  law_X0 : ∀ u, P.map (X0 u) = μ0 u
  brownian : ∀ u, Peng1990.SMP.IsStdBrownian P (B u)
  indep : iIndep (noiseFam X0 B) P

/-- The natural filtration `σ(Y(s) : s ≤ t)` of a process `Y` (intersected with the ambient
σ-algebra, which changes nothing when every `Y(s)` is measurable). -/
def filtOf {Ω : Type*} [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] {β : Type*} [mβ : MeasurableSpace β]
    (Y : ℝ≥0 → Ω → β) : Filtration ℝ≥0 mΩ where
  seq t := (⨆ s ≤ t, MeasurableSpace.comap (Y s) mβ) ⊓ mΩ
  mono' _ _ hst := inf_le_inf_right _ (iSup₂_le fun r hr => le_iSup₂_of_le r (hr.trans hst) le_rfl)
  le' _ := inf_le_right

/-- `𝓕ᵘ_t = σ(X_u(0), B_u(s) : s ≤ t)`. -/
def filtU {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (X0 : I → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (B : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin d → ℝ) (u : I) : Filtration ℝ≥0 ‹MeasurableSpace Ω› :=
  filtOf (fun t ω => (X0 u ω, B u t ω))

/-- `𝓕ⁿ_t = σ(ξⁿ, X_{j/n}(0), B_{j/n}(s) : j ≤ n, s ≤ t)`. -/
noncomputable def filtN {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (ξ : (n : ℕ) → Ω → Fin n → Fin n → ℝ)
    (X0 : I → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (B : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin d → ℝ) (n : ℕ) :
    Filtration ℝ≥0 ‹MeasurableSpace Ω› :=
  filtOf (fun t ω => (ξ n ω, fun j : Fin n => X0 (lab n j) ω, fun j : Fin n => B (lab n j) t ω))

/-! ### Coefficients and the graphon particle system (2.1), p. 3591 -/

/-- The graphon drift `∫_I ∫_{ℝᵈ} b(x, y) G(u,v) μ_{v,s}(dy) dv`, with `μ_{v,s} = ℒ(X_v(s))`. -/
noncomputable def graphonDrift {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (P : Measure Ω)
    (G : I → I → ℝ) (b : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (X : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (u : I) (s : ℝ≥0) (x : Fin d → ℝ) : Fin d → ℝ :=
  ∫ v, ∫ y, G u v • b x y ∂(P.map (X v s))

/-- The `(i, j)` entry of the graphon diffusion `∫_I ∫_{ℝᵈ} σ(x, y) G(u,v) μ_{v,s}(dy) dv`. -/
noncomputable def graphonDiff {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (P : Measure Ω)
    (G : I → I → ℝ) (sigma : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℝ)
    (X : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (u : I) (s : ℝ≥0) (x : Fin d → ℝ) (i j : Fin d) : ℝ :=
  ∫ v, ∫ y, G u v * sigma x y i j ∂(P.map (X v s))

/-- `X = (X_u : u ∈ I)` solves the graphon particle system (2.1) on `[0, T]`: continuous paths
starting at `X_u(0)`, law family in `ℳ`, and each `X_u − X_u(0)` an Itô process for the
filtration of `(X_u(0), B_u)`, driven by `B_u`, with the graphon drift and diffusion. -/
structure IsGraphonSolution {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (T : ℝ≥0) (P : Measure Ω)
    (X0 : I → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (B : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin d → ℝ) (G : I → I → ℝ)
    (b : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (sigma : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℝ)
    (X : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) : Prop where
  cont : ∀ u ω, Continuous (fun s : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ≥0) T => X u s ω)
  init : ∀ u ω, X u 0 ω = X0 u ω
  meas_path : ∀ u, AEMeasurable (pathOf T (X u)) P
  inM : InM (fun u => law T P (X u))
  sde : ∀ u, Peng1990.SMP.IsItoProcess (filtU X0 B u) P T (B u) (0 : Fin d → ℝ)
    (fun s ω => graphonDrift P G b X u s (X u s ω))
    (fun j s ω i => graphonDiff P G sigma X u s (X u s ω) i j)
    (fun t ω => X u t ω - X0 u ω)

/-! ### The n-particle system (3.1), p. 3594 -/

/-- `Xⁿ = (Xⁿ_1, …, Xⁿ_n)` solves (3.1) on `[0, T]`: particle `i` starts at `X_{i/n}(0)`, is
driven by `B_{i/n}`, and has drift `(1/n) Σⱼ ξⁿ_ij b(Xⁿ_i, Xⁿ_j)` and diffusion
`(1/n) Σⱼ ξⁿ_ij σ(Xⁿ_i, Xⁿ_j)`. -/
structure IsParticleSolution {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (T : ℝ≥0) (P : Measure Ω)
    (X0 : I → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (B : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin d → ℝ)
    (ξ : (n : ℕ) → Ω → Fin n → Fin n → ℝ)
    (b : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (sigma : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℝ)
    (n : ℕ) (Xn : Fin n → ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) : Prop where
  cont : ∀ i ω, Continuous (fun s : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ≥0) T => Xn i s ω)
  init : ∀ i ω, Xn i 0 ω = X0 (lab n i) ω
  meas_path : ∀ i, AEMeasurable (pathOf T (Xn i)) P
  sde : ∀ i, Peng1990.SMP.IsItoProcess (filtN ξ X0 B n) P T (B (lab n i)) (0 : Fin d → ℝ)
    (fun s ω => (1 / (n : ℝ)) • ∑ j, ξ n ω i j • b (Xn i s ω) (Xn j s ω))
    (fun j' s ω i' => (1 / (n : ℝ)) * ∑ j, ξ n ω i j * sigma (Xn i s ω) (Xn j s ω) i' j')
    (fun t ω => Xn i t ω - X0 (lab n i) ω)

/-! ### Conditions 2.1, 2.3 and 3.2 -/

/-- Condition 2.1 with exponent `2 + ε`: measurable initial laws with
`sup_u E|X_u(0)|^{2+ε} < ∞`, and `b`, `σ` Lipschitz (σ measured entrywise). -/
def Cond21 {d : ℕ} (ε : ℝ) (μ0 : I → Measure (Fin d → ℝ))
    (b : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (sigma : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℝ) : Prop :=
  Measurable μ0 ∧ (∀ u, IsProbabilityMeasure (μ0 u)) ∧
    (⨆ u, ∫⁻ x, ‖x‖ₑ ^ (2 + ε) ∂(μ0 u)) < ⊤ ∧
    ∃ K : ℝ, 0 ≤ K ∧ ∀ x x' y y' : Fin d → ℝ,
      ‖b x y - b x' y'‖ + ‖Peng1990.SMP.matEntries (sigma x y - sigma x' y')‖ ≤
        K * (‖x - x'‖ + ‖y - y'‖)

/-- Condition 2.3 for the finite family of intervals `J` covering `I`: there is `κ₀ > 0` with
`W₂(μ_{u₁}(0), μ_{u₂}(0)) ≤ κ₀|u₁ − u₂|` on each `J i` and
`|G(u₁,v₁) − G(u₂,v₂)| ≤ κ₀(|u₁ − u₂| + |v₁ − v₂|)` on each block `J i × J j`. -/
def Cond23 {d N : ℕ} (μ0 : I → Measure (Fin d → ℝ)) (G : I → I → ℝ) (J : Fin N → Set I) :
    Prop :=
  (∀ i, Set.OrdConnected (J i)) ∧ (⋃ i, J i) = Set.univ ∧
    ∃ κ₀ : ℝ, 0 < κ₀ ∧
      (∀ i, ∀ u₁ ∈ J i, ∀ u₂ ∈ J i,
        W2 (μ0 u₁) (μ0 u₂) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (κ₀ * |(u₁ : ℝ) - u₂|)) ∧
      ∀ i j, ∀ u₁ ∈ J i, ∀ u₂ ∈ J i, ∀ v₁ ∈ J j, ∀ v₂ ∈ J j,
        |G u₁ v₁ - G u₂ v₂| ≤ κ₀ * (|(u₁ : ℝ) - u₂| + |(v₁ : ℝ) - v₂|)

/-- Bernoulli edge weights: `ξ_ij = ξ_ji ∈ {0, 1}`, `P(ξ_ij = 1) = p_ij`, and
`{ξ_ij : i ≤ j}` (diagonal included) mutually independent. -/
def BernoulliEdges {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {n : ℕ} (P : Measure Ω)
    (ξ : Ω → Fin n → Fin n → ℝ) (p : Fin n → Fin n → ℝ) : Prop :=
  Measurable ξ ∧ (∀ ω i j, ξ ω i j = ξ ω j i) ∧ (∀ ω i j, ξ ω i j = 0 ∨ ξ ω i j = 1) ∧
    (∀ i j, P {ω | ξ ω i j = 1} = ENNReal.ofReal (p i j)) ∧
    iIndepFun (fun (q : {q : Fin n × Fin n // q.1 ≤ q.2}) ω => ξ ω q.1.1 q.1.2) P

/-- Condition 3.2: either (i) `ξⁿ_ij = G(i/n, j/n)` for all `n, i, j`, or (ii) for all `n`,
`ξⁿ_ij = ξⁿ_ji = Bernoulli(G(i/n, j/n))` independently for `i ≤ j`, independent of
`{B_u, X_u(0) : u ∈ I}`. -/
def Cond32 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (P : Measure Ω)
    (X0 : I → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (B : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → Fin d → ℝ)
    (ξ : (n : ℕ) → Ω → Fin n → Fin n → ℝ) (G : I → I → ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ n ω i j, ξ n ω i j = G (lab n i) (lab n j)) ∨
    ∀ n, BernoulliEdges P (ξ n) (fun i j => G (lab n i) (lab n j)) ∧
      Indep (MeasurableSpace.comap (ξ n) inferInstance) (noiseSigma X0 B) P

/-! ### The three terms of (6.16), p. 3609 (particle `i`, time `s`) -/

/-- `T̃^{n,1}_s = E|(1/n) Σⱼ ξⁿ_ij (b(Xⁿ_i(s), Xⁿ_j(s)) − b(X_{i/n}(s), X_{j/n}(s)))|²`. -/
noncomputable def Tt1 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (P : Measure Ω)
    (ξ : (n : ℕ) → Ω → Fin n → Fin n → ℝ) (b : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (X : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (n : ℕ) (Xn : Fin n → ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (i : Fin n) (s : ℝ≥0) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∫⁻ ω, ‖(1 / (n : ℝ)) • ∑ j, ξ n ω i j •
      (b (Xn i s ω) (Xn j s ω) - b (X (lab n i) s ω) (X (lab n j) s ω))‖ₑ ^ 2 ∂P

/-- `T̃^{n,2}_s = E|(1/n) Σⱼ (ξⁿ_ij b(X_{i/n}(s), X_{j/n}(s))
− ∫ b(X_{i/n}(s), x) G(i/n, j/n) μ_{j/n,s}(dx))|²`. -/
noncomputable def Tt2 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (P : Measure Ω)
    (ξ : (n : ℕ) → Ω → Fin n → Fin n → ℝ) (G : I → I → ℝ)
    (b : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (X : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (n : ℕ) (i : Fin n) (s : ℝ≥0) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∫⁻ ω, ‖(1 / (n : ℝ)) • ∑ j, (ξ n ω i j • b (X (lab n i) s ω) (X (lab n j) s ω) -
      ∫ x, G (lab n i) (lab n j) • b (X (lab n i) s ω) x ∂(P.map (X (lab n j) s)))‖ₑ ^ 2 ∂P

/-- `T̃^{n,3}_s = E|(1/n) Σⱼ ∫ b(X_{i/n}(s), x) G(i/n, j/n) μ_{j/n,s}(dx)
− ∫_I ∫ b(X_{i/n}(s), x) G(i/n, v) μ_{v,s}(dx) dv|²`. -/
noncomputable def Tt3 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {d : ℕ} (P : Measure Ω)
    (G : I → I → ℝ) (b : (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ) → (Fin d → ℝ))
    (X : I → ℝ≥0 → Ω → (Fin d → ℝ)) (n : ℕ) (i : Fin n) (s : ℝ≥0) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∫⁻ ω, ‖(1 / (n : ℝ)) • ∑ j, ∫ x, G (lab n i) (lab n j) • b (X (lab n i) s ω) x
      ∂(P.map (X (lab n j) s)) - graphonDrift P G b X (lab n i) s (X (lab n i) s ω)‖ₑ ^ 2 ∂P

end GraphonMF.DenseRate


